  <!-- Two Gaps Section ******************* -->
  <Content
    id="problem"
    tagline="WHY IN-STORE FALLS BEHIND"
    title="Two gaps are draining physical retail."
    subtitle="E-commerce wins on convenience and intelligence. Stores lose on both — every day, in every aisle."
  >
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 p-6 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide bg-red-50 text-red-600 mb-4">
            The sales gap
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Friction kills baskets.</h3>
          <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
            Shoppers can't find products. Aisles are confusing. Out-of-stocks aren't visible until they're at the shelf.
            Lines slow checkout. Every friction point is a smaller basket — or an abandoned trip.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 p-6 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide bg-amber-50 text-amber-600 mb-4">
            The intent gap
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">You see what was bought, not what was wanted.</h3>
          <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-300">
            E-commerce captures every search, every browse, every abandoned cart. Stores capture transactions — and only
            after the customer decided, or gave up. The data gap compounds every day.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div
        class="max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-6 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 px-6 py-4 flex items-start gap-4 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900"
      >
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 dark:text-slate-500 mt-0.5 shrink-0"
          >The root</span
        >
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-slate-200 font-medium">
          Both gaps share one cause: there's no intelligence layer between the shopper and the shelf.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS Section ******************* -->
  <Content
    id="how-it-works"
    tagline="HOW IT WORKS"
    title="One product. <span class='text-gradient'>Two compounding wins.</span>"
    subtitle="Shoppers use AislePal because it's faster. That's how you build the data foundation no competitor can replicate."
  >
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <img
        src={howItWorks.src}
        alt="AislePal how it works — four steps"
        class="mx-auto w-full rounded-lg"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Analytics Features Section ******************* -->
  <!-- <Features
    id="features"
    tagline="Aisle Analytics"
    title="See what you've been <span class='text-gradient'>missing</span>"
    subtitle="AislePal Analytics turns in-store behavior into actionable insight."
    columns={3}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Search Intelligence',
        description:
          "Know exactly what customers are looking for — including products you don't carry yet. Identify demand gaps before they become lost sales.",
        icon: 'tabler:search',
      },
      {
        title: 'Conversion Tracking',
        description:
          'See the journey from search to shelf to checkout. Understand where customers convert, abandon, or substitute.',
        icon: 'tabler:eye',
      },
      {
        title: 'Out-of-Stock Impact',
        description:
          "Measure the real cost of stockouts. See what customers searched for, couldn't find, and what they did next.",
        icon: 'tabler:shopping-cart-off',
      },
      {
        title: 'Navigation Patterns',
        description:
          'Understand how customers move through your store. Identify high-traffic zones and optimize product placement.',
        icon: 'tabler:map-pin',
      },
      {
        title: 'Promotion Performance',
        description:
          'Track promotion engagement from impression to purchase. Know which offers drive action and which get ignored.',
        icon: 'tabler:trending-up',
      },
      {
        title: 'Demand Forecasting',
        description:
          'Use search and browse data to predict demand before it shows up at the register. Plan inventory based on intent, not just history.',
        icon: 'tabler:chart-bar',
      },
    ]}
  /> -->

  <!-- Two Sides Section ******************* -->
  <Content
    tagline="WHAT EACH SIDE GETS"
    title="Built for the aisle. <span class='text-gradient'>Built for the dashboard.</span>"
    subtitle="AislePal is one product with two interfaces — the shopper-facing web app, and the retailer-facing intelligence platform."
  >
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 p-6 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">For shoppers</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mb-6">Convenience that feels like online.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            {
              [
                {
                  icon: 'tabler:search',
                  title: 'Discover',
                  body: 'Search naturally — "organic milk under $6." See what\'s in stock, ranked, and on promotion.',
                },
                {
                  icon: 'tabler:map-pin',
                  title: 'Navigate',
                  body: 'Aisle-level guidance to every product. No more wandering, no more giving up.',
                },
                {
                  icon: 'tabler:shopping-cart',
                  title: 'Check out',
                  body: 'Optional in-aisle scan-and-pay. Skip the line. Faster trips, fuller carts.',
                },
              ].map(({ icon, title, body }) => (
                <div class="flex gap-4">
                  <div class="w-9 h-9 shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-[#4b9ea5]/10">
                    <Icon name={icon} class="w-5 h-5 text-[#4b9ea5]" />
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold mb-1">{title}</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted dark:text-slate-300">{body}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-slate-700 p-6 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-1">For your store</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted dark:text-slate-400 mb-6">The intent layer e-commerce has had for 20 years.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            {
              [
                {
                  icon: 'tabler:bulb',
                  title: 'Search intelligence',
                  body: "Know what shoppers wanted — including products you don't carry. Identify lost sales before they become lost customers.",
                },
                {
                  icon: 'tabler:route',
                  title: 'Navigation patterns',
                  body: 'See how shoppers actually move through the store. Where they slow down, where they give up. Optimize layout based on behavior.',
                },
                {
                  icon: 'tabler:chart-bar',
                  title: 'Demand forecasting',
                  body: 'Use search and browse signals to predict demand before it hits the register. Plan inventory on intent, not just history.',
                },
              ].map(({ icon, title, body }) => (
                <div class="flex gap-4">
                  <div class="w-9 h-9 shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-[#4b9ea5]/10">
                    <Icon name={icon} class="w-5 h-5 text-[#4b9ea5]" />
                  </div>
                  <div>
                    <p class="font-semibold mb-1">{title}</p>
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted dark:text-slate-300">{body}</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Financial Case Section ******************* -->
  <Stats
    id="results"
    tagline="THE FINANCIAL CASE"
    title="Pays for itself in quarter one. <span class='text-gradient'>Compounds for years after.</span>"
    subtitle="AislePal delivers measurable sales lift on day one. The intent data it captures becomes a strategic asset that grows in value with every shopper."
    stats={[
      { title: 'Average basket size increase', amount: '23%' },
      { title: 'Improvement in promotion ROI', amount: '31%' },
      { title: 'Reduction in stockout impact', amount: '23%' },
      { title: 'Increase in customer insights vs loyalty data', amount: '2.4×' },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- Deployment Timeline Section ******************* -->
  <Content
    id="setup"
    tagline="DEPLOYMENT"
    title="Live in two weeks. <span class='text-gradient'>No construction required.</span>"
    subtitle="AislePal deploys without hardware installation, store modification, or six-month IT projects."
  >
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <img
        src={deploymentTimeline.src}
        alt="AislePal deployment timeline — Setup, Integration, Customization, Deployment over 14 days"
        class="mx-auto w-full rounded-lg"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Integrations Section ******************* -->
  <Content
    id="integrations"
    isReversed
    tagline="INTEGRATIONS"
    title="Plugs into the systems <span class='text-gradient'>you already run.</span>"
    subtitle="POS, ERP, inventory, and loyalty — connected in days, not months."
  >
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <img
        src={erpIntegrations.src}
        alt="AislePal integration diagram"
        class="mx-auto w-full rounded-lg"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Industries Section ******************* -->
  <Industries
    id="industries"
    tagline="INDUSTRIES"
    title="Who we're <span class='text-gradient'>built for</span>"
    subtitle=""
    industries={[
      { name: 'Grocery', image: '~/assets/images/industries/supermarket-aisle.jpg' },
      { name: 'Big Box', image: '~/assets/images/industries/big-box.png' },
      { name: 'Department', image: '~/assets/images/industries/department.png' },
      { name: 'Pharmacy', image: '~/assets/images/industries/pharmacy.png' },
      { name: 'Specialty', image: '~/assets/images/industries/speciality.png' },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- FAQs Section ******************* -->
  <FAQs
    id="faq"
    tagline="FAQ"
    title="Questions, <span class='text-gradient'>honestly answered.</span>"
    subtitle="Common questions from retail decision-makers evaluating AislePal."
    columns={1}
    classes={{ container: 'max-w-4xl' }}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'How fast do retailers see basket lift?',
        description:
          'Most pilots see measurable basket-size lift within the first 30 days, driven by easier product discovery and reduced abandonment. The biggest gains arrive in months 2–3 as recommendations and promotions tune to live behavioral data.',
        icon: 'tabler:chevron-down',
      },
      {
        title: 'Who owns the data — us or AislePal?',
        description:
          'You do. Always. AislePal is the infrastructure that captures and structures your in-store intent data, but every byte belongs to your business. Full export at any time, no lock-in.',
        icon: 'tabler:chevron-down',
      },
      {
        title: 'How does this comply with CCPA and GDPR?',
        description:
          'AislePal is privacy-first by design. No persistent shopper IDs unless explicitly opted in via your loyalty program. Anonymous session-based capture by default. Data residency, retention windows, and deletion are all configurable per region.',
        icon: 'tabler:chevron-down',
      },
      {
        title: "What happens if a shopper doesn't want to scan the QR?",
        description:
          "The store works exactly as it does today. AislePal is purely additive — never required, never gated. Shoppers who scan get a better trip; everyone else shops normally. There's no downside to non-adoption.",
        icon: 'tabler:chevron-down',
      },
      {
        title: 'Do we need new hardware?',
        description:
          "No. AislePal runs entirely on shoppers' phones via a web app. The only physical change is QR codes at entrances and key shelf locations — printed, mounted, done.",
        icon: 'tabler:chevron-down',
      },
      {
        title: 'How does this fit alongside our existing loyalty program?',
        description:
          'It enhances it. Loyalty programs tell you who bought what. AislePal tells you what they searched, considered, and skipped. Linked together, they become the most complete picture of an in-store shopper any retailer has ever had.',
        icon: 'tabler:chevron-down',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- CallToAction Widget *********** -->
  <CallToAction
    id="contact"
    actions={[
      {
        variant: 'primary',
        text: 'Book a Demo',
        href: 'https://calendly.com/abdulla-aislepal/30min',
        icon: 'tabler:calendar',
      },
      {
        variant: 'secondary',
        text: 'Join a Pilot',
        href: 'https://calendly.com/abdulla-aislepal/30min',
        icon: 'tabler:users',
      },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Bring the advantage back to your <span class="text-gradient">store.</span>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      Faster trips today. Smarter decisions forever.
    </Fragment>
  </CallToAction>
</Layout>
